/*  Author Alexander Pitzer
    ETH Zurich
    Copyright (C) 2025 Alexander Pitzer

    Solubility equilibrium database and helper functions.
    Analogous structure to acidbase.mac.

    Database format: association list
    index = salt (string, mhchem-compatible)
      value = [pKsp, cation, cation_count, anion, anion_count]

    Ksp is always computed from pKsp: Ksp = 10^(-pKsp)
    This avoids rounding errors from storing both values.

    CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics — Table of solubility product constants
    NIST Standard Reference Database — Critically evaluated stability constants
    Lange's Handbook of Chemistry — Solubility product table
    Atkins' Physical Chemistry or Zumdahl's Chemistry textbook appendices
    IUPAC-NIST Solubility Data Series
*/

/* Restructured to a genuine Maxima hashed array: one indexed assignment per
   salt, giving O(1) lookup instead of a linear assoc() scan. */
    /* --- Halides --- */
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["AgCl"] : [9.75,  "Ag^+",      1, "Cl^-",  1]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["AgBr"] : [12.27, "Ag^+",      1, "Br^-",  1]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["AgI"] : [16.07, "Ag^+",      1, "I^-",   1]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["AgF"] : [0.69,  "Ag^+",      1, "F^-",   1]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["CuCl"] : [6.76,  "Cu^+",      1, "Cl^-",  1]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["PbCl2"] : [4.77,  "Pb^{2+}",   1, "Cl^-",  2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["PbBr2"] : [5.18,  "Pb^{2+}",   1, "Br^-",  2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["PbI2"] : [8.01,  "Pb^{2+}",   1, "I^-",   2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["PbF2"] : [7.48,  "Pb^{2+}",   1, "F^-",   2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["CaF2"] : [10.46, "Ca^{2+}",   1, "F^-",   2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["BaF2"] : [6.74,  "Ba^{2+}",   1, "F^-",   2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["MgF2"] : [10.29, "Mg^{2+}",   1, "F^-",   2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["SrF2"] : [8.36,  "Sr^{2+}",   1, "F^-",   2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["Hg2Cl2"] : [17.84, "Hg2^{2+}",  1, "Cl^-",  2]$
%_SOLUBILITY_DB["Hg2Br2"] : [22.19, "Hg2^{2+}",  1, "Br^-",  2]$
